
> pi-model-discoverer@0.1.0 test
> tsx --test test/*.test.ts

✔ configuration validates defaults and rejects unsafe or credential-bearing inputs (0.787333ms)
✔ normalization deduplicates, preserves explicit metadata, and uses conservative defaults (0.374625ms)
✔ discovery sends saved key only to the configured origin with redirects blocked (10.979875ms)
✔ Anthropic catalogs use x-api-key and paginate without following server URLs (0.442459ms)
✔ failures never expose response bodies, URLs, or credential-bearing errors (6.92225ms)
✔ malformed saved keys cannot escape through header validation errors (0.663167ms)
✔ cancellation does not issue a request (0.232542ms)
✔ native Pi login, refresh, failure retention, and logout work without credential-file access (1.8475ms)
✔ offline refresh and rejected publication do not replace in-memory catalogs (0.439917ms)
✔ Pi's actual extension loader registers the command and custom provider without auth files (116.034416ms)
✔ native discovery delegates to Pi, selecting only authenticated dynamic providers (0.846541ms)
✔ explicit unknown and unauthenticated providers do not cause a refresh (0.088084ms)
✔ refresh reports per-provider failures without leaking native auth errors (0.112167ms)
✔ cancelled refresh is not reported as successful (0.071958ms)
✔ a silently superseded refresh does not claim that new models were published (0.090792ms)
